 "title": "Reverse Swell",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a sound that swells up out of nothing and stops short, like a tape played backwards: the 'reverse cymbal' build before a hit.\n\nHow it's built: a long ATTACK (1.5 s) and an almost instant RELEASE on the volume, and a filter envelope that opens over the same time, so each note grows brighter and louder and then cuts off when you let go; a small Reverb after, kept short so the stop stays sharp. Six voices.\n\nPlay: hold a chord for a beat or two and let go on the downbeat.\n\nTweak: the two ATTACKs (keep them together), the reverb's SIZE and MIX (more blurs the stop).",
